<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Parler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1300–c. 1370</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Heinrich Parler the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Parler was a German master builder from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> who worked in Schwäbisch Gmünd, where from 1351 he built the choir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-minster">Holy Cross Minster</a>, one of the first late Gothic hall churches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He founded the Parler family of architects and sculptors; his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-parler">Peter Parler</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-vitus-cathedral">St. Vitus Cathedral</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-parler.jpg" alt="Heinrich Parler" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beckstet at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gmuend_Muenster_von_Suedwest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
